{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994441-legacies-to-mystery-cults","id":994441,"title":"Legacies to Mystery Cults","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-27T23:49:15-07:00","id":994441,"title":"Legacies to Mystery Cults","content":"Has anyone tried turning any of Mage's legacies into blue book-suitable Mystery Cults? My first idea was to turn the Cult of the Doomsday Clock into a God-Machine cult. Any others that you think would work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T07:37:41-07:00","id":994568,"title":"","content":"Tremere Liches as a group of Ghouls who've learned a weaker, rudimentary version of Diablerie that lets them eat mortal souls in place of Vitae?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:28:17-07:00","id":994784,"title":"","content":"I was actually thinking of going full circle and having the Tremere be a Bloodline again.<br /> <br /> For Bloodline gift, I'd say that they can learn any mortal sorcery, Theban Sorcery, or Cruac spell regardless of Covenant. Maybe also give them some Devotions related to sorcery- making it easier, detecting it, countering it, etc. <br /> <br /> I'd carry over the original weakness, and say that they're widely hated and distrusted and have to keep their Bloodline membership a secret. Maybe also add a weakness that they have to consume souls or commit diablerie to retain their powers, and that's why they're so distrusted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-28-2016, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:17:27-07:00","id":994831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994441-legacies-to-mystery-cults?p=994784#post994784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually thinking of going full circle and having the Tremere be a Bloodline again.<br /> <br /> For Bloodline gift, I'd say that they can learn any mortal sorcery, Theban Sorcery, or Cruac spell regardless of Covenant. Maybe also give them some Devotions related to sorcery- making it easier, detecting it, countering it, etc.<br /> <br /> I'd carry over the original weakness, and say that they're widely hated and distrusted and have to keep their Bloodline membership a secret. Maybe also add a weakness that they have to consume souls or commit diablerie to retain their powers, and that's why they're so distrusted.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about<b></b>: Their Bloodline Gift lets them copy the special powers of other &quot;magic&quot; users (see Show Of Power as a base) <i>OR</i> lets them acquire near versions as Devotions (which means they have to cough up the XP for each new power). Their curse is they need the Vitae of the being whose power they are copying in their system. Want Cruac/Theban? Time to wrestle with Vitae addiction! Want Arcana? Hope you know a Mage who likes the Kiss! Pretty soon, no one is going to like them.<br /> <br /> You can make it worse by them not able to form a Vinculum with supernaturals (so no easy donors). Or even harsher by requiring that they can only spend those Vitae on their stolen powers (so they can't just bank a few points, and say they are burning &quot;normal&quot; Vitae to active them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:52:32-07:00","id":994863,"title":"","content":"I kind of came up with an idea I liked in the other thread, that isn't as crossover reliant. <br /> <br /> Back on topic, what other legacies would work as mystery cults?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:21:06-07:00","id":995009,"title":"","content":"Every Legacy is suitable for it, really. Just pick a central theme and run with it. The Elemental Tamers become elementalists dedicated around the symbolism of a given element; Dreamspeakers produce astral divers; the Scions of God become spiritualists...<br /> <br /> Most Legacies are based off of real magical traditions of one sort or another; the easiest path is to just try and find the original source of inspiration and base a cult off that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:27:50-07:00","id":995013,"title":"","content":"Well, the primary criterion I'm operating on is spookiness- which ones feel the most cult-y and creepy? <br /> <br /> The Seers are another one I'm going to include. I'm going to have their attainments be based all on avoiding having their memories or trails and so on read supernaturally, allowing them to stay hidden. <br /> <br /> I do want at least one dream-focused mystery cult, since I want to do something with the Astral. Lemme write up a list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:34:29-07:00","id":995017,"title":"","content":"The Eleventh Question fits right snugly into a supernatural mystery. As a Mystery Cult, it becomes a secret society of mystic detectives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:54:42-07:00","id":995025,"title":"","content":"Here's the list of the ones I'm going for:<br /> <br /> The Cult of the Doomsday Clock: I'm having them by God-Machine focused by default, keeping their time fuckery. <br /> Morphean Continuity: I wanted some astral stuff, so I'm keeping them. They're related to the schemes of the dream entities described in Dancers in the Dusk. <br /> The Legion: Keeping the &quot;replace your limbs with alien monsters&quot; thing, but with the twist that they're quite pleasant and treat their eldritch abomination worship as a mostly Sundays and holidays thing. <br /> Oneironauts: Something something I need another astral one. <br /> Threnodists: I just think their deal with the physics machinery is cool. <br /> Orphans of Proteus: <br /> Ascended Adepts: They focus on mastering their Oneiroi, dreams, and shedding their physical forms. <br /> The Scions of God: I want to do some stuff with mortal spiritualists, so I'm gonna have several spirit Mystery Cults. <br /> The Neocologists: Mad scientists and techno-spiritualists studying how spirits interact with the material world. <br /> The Nemesis Scholars: This and the lower one aren't Legacies, but I'm adapting two of the coolest Abyssals into mystery cults. <br /> The Vassals of Leaves: See above. <br /> The Seers of the Throne: Not actually a Legacy, but I'm making them into a Mystery Cult/conspiracy. <br /> Tremere: I'm making them into a Bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}